History (what the film simplifies)
- The Malayan Union was inaugurated on 1 April 1946 over the Malay states, Penang and Malacca (Singapore stayed a
  separate colony). Malay opposition, led by the newly founded UMNO, ended it; the Federation of Malaya replaced it
  on 1 February 1948.
- The London conference (January–February 1956) agreed that the Federation would be independent by August 1957 "if
  possible"; independence came on 31 August 1957. It was negotiated, not won in a war of independence. The Malayan
  Emergency (1948–1960), a communist insurgency, ran alongside and is not shown.
- Kuala Lumpur was the capital. Singapore remained a British colony in 1957.
